    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA Eoin Dillon is delighted to bring to market this derelict home with outbuildings, set in the breathtaking countryside of Kilcommon, Co. Tipperary.\n\nThe house, which requires full restoration also features outbuildings with significant potential for conversion to serve a variety of uses such as artist`s studio, yoga retreat, etc. Located in a peaceful, rural setting, it is surrounded by beautiful nature walks and trails.\n\nThe entire property offers an ideal project for those looking to create their dream home in a serene environment. Whether you envision a complete rebuild or a thoughtful restoration, the expansive site and surrounding landscape provide an inspiring backdrop.\n\nBuyers may be eligible for grants of up to 70,000 through the Cro Cnaithe Fund, and additional support of up to 26,750 under the Sustainable Energy Authority of Ireland`s Better Energy Homes Scheme. These grants make this property an attractive option for those looking to invest in a restoration project while reducing overall costs.\n\nThe property is situated just 1km from Kilcommon village, with Nenagh (22km), Limerick City (38 km), Newport (18km) and Thurles (28km) offering a variety of amenities.\n\nNo access to the house granted to members of the public. We can facilitate access to engineer/builder with safe pass, insurance and PPE.\n\nEntrance hallway - 1.36m (4'6) x 1.3m (4'3)\n\nLiving room - 5.12m (16'10) x 5.08m (16'8)\n\nSitting room - 5.03m (16'6) x 4.83m (15'10)\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.02m (9'11) x 1.93m (6'4)\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.05m (10'0) x 2.99m (9'10)\n\nBedroom 3 - 5m (16'5) x 2.94m (9'8)\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.08m (10'1) x 1.81m (5'11)\n\nBedroom 5 - 3.87m (12'8) x 2.33m (7'8)\n\nBedroom 6 - 5.09m (16'8) x 4.83m (15'10)\n\n\nDirections\nFrom Nenagh, travel on the R497 past Costello`s shop for 8 km and at the T- junction in Dolla take the left and the next right at Lackin`s shop. Take the R497 for 2.9 km and stay to right. At Curreeny Cross take a right. Continue for 4.1km (passing Curreeny Church) and the property is on your left. Nearest house Eircode E41 F1C2\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      }
    ],
